---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Row from '../../components/Row.astro';
import { COMPANY, TIP_LINE } from '../../data/site';

// The problems people actually met in our live tests (sessions 59 and 64,
// CONNECT-APPS-DESIGN.md), each answered first, in the app's own words.
const OUTLINE = [
  { id: 'not-using', title: "My AI app doesn't use Zaaheen" },
  { id: 'not-listed', title: "My app isn't in the Agents tab" },
  { id: 'chatgpt', title: "ChatGPT can't see Zaaheen" },
  { id: 'claude', title: "Claude didn't ask to install" },
  { id: 'unknown-publisher', title: 'Windows says the publisher is unknown' },
  { id: 'mac-applications', title: 'The Mac says to move Zaaheen to Applications' },
  { id: 'mac-keychain', title: 'The Mac asks about the keychain' },
  { id: 'stopped', title: 'My apps stopped using Zaaheen' },
  { id: 'else', title: 'Something else went wrong' },
];
---
<Guide
  path="/docs/troubleshooting/"
  lede="Most problems come from an AI app looking only in its own memory, or not being connected yet. Each fix below starts with the answer. If yours isn't here, email us an activity record from Settings."
  outline={OUTLINE}
>
  <section class="docs-section">
    <Row level={2} id="not-using" title="My AI app answers without using Zaaheen" where="Claude, ChatGPT">
      <p>Claude and ChatGPT look in their own memory first and may stop there. Add this line to
         Claude's personal preferences, or to ChatGPT's Custom instructions, and they check Zaaheen as
         well:</p>
      <pre><code>{TIP_LINE}</code></pre>
      <p>You can also ask directly, for example "check my Zaaheen memory for how I like meetings
         booked". Cursor checks Zaaheen by itself when you ask about yourself.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="not-listed" title="My app isn't in the Agents tab" where="Agents">
      <p>An app shows in the <em>Agents</em> tab only while it is open and connected. Open the app,
         then check its own settings: each connection guide has a "Check it worked" step
         (<a href="/docs/connect-claude/">Claude</a>, <a href="/docs/connect-cursor/">Cursor</a>,
         <a href="/docs/connect-chatgpt/">ChatGPT</a>). If Zaaheen isn't listed there, connect it
         again.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="chatgpt" title="ChatGPT can't see Zaaheen" where="ChatGPT">
      <p>Use ChatGPT's Work or Codex mode: its Chat mode can't connect to apps on your computer. Then
         check the setting: <code>mcp</code> and <code>serve</code> must be two separate items under
         Arguments, not one line. See <a href="/docs/connect-chatgpt/">Connect ChatGPT</a>.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="claude" title="Claude didn't ask me to install Zaaheen" where="Claude › Extensions">
      <p>Zaaheen saves the extension to your Downloads folder. In Claude, open Settings, then
         Extensions, then Advanced settings, then Install Extension, and choose
         "Zaaheen for Claude.mcpb".</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="unknown-publisher" title="Windows says the publisher is unknown" where="Installer">
      <p>Choose <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>. Zaaheen is in beta and its installer is
         not code-signed yet; signing comes before the full launch.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="mac-applications" title="My Mac says to move Zaaheen to Applications" where="Mac">
      <p>Zaaheen runs only from the Applications folder. If you opened it from the disk image or
         from Downloads, quit it, drag Zaaheen into Applications in Finder, then open it from
         there.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="mac-keychain" title="My Mac asks whether Zaaheen can use the keychain" where="Mac">
      <p>The key to your memories is kept in your Mac's keychain, so macOS asks before Zaaheen
         reads it. Choose <em>Always Allow</em>. If Zaaheen says it couldn't use this computer's
         secure storage, open Keychain Access, unlock your login keychain, then try again.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="stopped" title="My apps stopped using Zaaheen" where="Settings › Account">
      <p>If your free trial or subscription has ended, Zaaheen stops serving your AI apps until you
         subscribe. Nothing is deleted: your memories stay on your computer, and <em>Download my
         memories</em> keeps working. Choose <em>Subscribe</em> in the app, and your apps pick
         Zaaheen up again.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="else" title="Something else went wrong" where="Settings › Help">
      <p>Choose <em>Save activity record…</em> in Settings, then email the file to
         <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with what you were doing. The record
         contains none of your memories.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>
</Guide>
